# The countersignature log is append-only and every row is self-contained:
# it carries its own timestamp, head and signature, so a verifier reads rows
# independently. Union-merge concatenates both sides instead of raising a
# conflict when the local cron and GitHub Actions both append. Git warns that
# union leaves added lines "in random order" -- harmless here, because order
# carries no meaning in this file.
witness-state/countersignatures.jsonl merge=union

# NOT union: union-merging JSON produces invalid JSON. Either side is safe,
# because a stale head only makes the next consistency proof span further back.
witness-state/last-heads.json -merge
